{"name":"Nonthal","status":"ok","title":"Nonthal","pageId":13982,"html":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" dir=\"ltr\" lang=\"en\"><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n</p><aside class=\"portable-infobox pi-background pi-border-color pi-theme-frwiki pi-layout-default type-location\" role=\"region\">\n\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Category:Maps_of_Nonthal\" title=\"Category:Maps of Nonthal\">Gallery</a></nav>\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-item-spacing pi-title pi-secondary-background\" data-source=\"name\">Nonthal</h2>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Geography</h2>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"type\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Type</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">City</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"region\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Region</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Turmish\" title=\"Turmish\">Turmish</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Vilhon_Reach\" title=\"Vilhon Reach\">Vilhon Reach</a></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"size\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Size</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Large<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRCG-p184_1-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCG-p184-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Society</h2>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"races\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Races</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Human\" title=\"Human\">Humans</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/Half-elves\" title=\"Half-elves\">half-elves</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Gnome\" title=\"Gnome\">gnomes</a><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-VR-p21_2-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-VR-p21-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Nonthal_3-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Nonthal-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Commerce</h2>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"imports\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Imports</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Animals</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"exports\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Exports</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Leather\" title=\"Leather\">Leather</a>, meat<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRCS3-p221_4-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS3-p221-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">History</h2>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"population1\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Population</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">12,902<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRCS3-p221_4-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS3-p221-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> in <a href=\"/wiki/1372_DR\" title=\"1372 DR\">1372 DR</a><br/>14,000<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRCG-p184_1-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCG-p184-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> in <a href=\"/wiki/1479_DR\" title=\"1479 DR\">1479 DR</a></div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvQ2F0ZWdvcnk6SW5oYWJpdGFudHNfb2ZfTm9udGhhbD9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\" title=\"Category:Inhabitants of Nonthal (page does not exist)\">Inhabitants of  Nonthal</span></nav>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><a class=\"newcategory\" href=\"/wiki/Category:Locations_in_Nonthal\" title=\"Category:Locations in Nonthal\">Locations in  Nonthal</a></nav>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvQ2F0ZWdvcnk6T3JnYW5pemF0aW9uc19pbl9Ob250aGFsP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\" title=\"Category:Organizations in Nonthal (page does not exist)\">Organizations in  Nonthal</span></nav>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><span class=\"DPL-purge plainlinks\"><a class=\"text\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Template:Category_intersection_jump?DPL_cat1=Locations_in__Nonthal&amp;DPL_cat2=Roads&amp;action=purge\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Roads  in  Nonthal</a></span></nav>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvQ2F0ZWdvcnk6Rm9vZF9hbmRfZHJpbmtfZnJvbV9Ob250aGFsP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\" title=\"Category:Food and drink from Nonthal (page does not exist)\">Food and drink from  Nonthal</span></nav>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvQ2F0ZWdvcnk6SXRlbXNfZnJvbV9Ob250aGFsP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\" title=\"Category:Items from Nonthal (page does not exist)\">Items from  Nonthal</span></nav>\n</aside>\n<p class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></p><p><b>Nonthal</b> was a city, reputed for being the most peaceful and stable in the nation of <a href=\"/wiki/Turmish\" title=\"Turmish\">Turmish</a>, in the <a href=\"/wiki/Vilhon_Reach\" title=\"Vilhon Reach\">Vilhon Reach</a>.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRCG-p184_1-2\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCG-p184-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<div aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\" class=\"toc\" id=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\"><input class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" role=\"button\" style=\"display:none\" type=\"checkbox\"/><div class=\"toctitle\" dir=\"ltr\" lang=\"en\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Description\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Description</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Geography\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Geography</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Trade\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Trade</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#History\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">History</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Notable_Locations\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Notable Locations</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Inhabitants\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Inhabitants</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Appendix\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Appendix</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Gallery\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Gallery</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Appearances\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Appearances</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#References\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">References</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Connections\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Connections</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Description\">Description</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Description\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Nonthal?veaction=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Description\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The citizens of Nonthal loved the city's stability and attempted to stay out of conflicts if possible. For that reason, the numerous adventurers that passed through were often met with cold shoulder<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRCG-p184_1-3\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCG-p184-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> and the overwhelming stench of the town's cattle industries.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRCS3-p221_4-2\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS3-p221-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>The city itself was quite dull in appearance. Its streets were filled with market stalls and tradesmen.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-poly106_5-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-poly106-5\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>The city had a functioning <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/Sewer_system\" title=\"Sewer system\">sewer system</a>, that was fixed, expanded, and improved by <span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvSm9zdGVyX0JhcmJlbGxvdz9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\" title=\"Joster Barbellow (page does not exist)\">Joster Barbellow</span>, of the <span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvQmFyYmVsbG93P2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\" title=\"Barbellow (page does not exist)\">Barbellow</span> <a href=\"/wiki/Gnome\" title=\"Gnome\">gnome</a> family. The \"Lord of the Sewers\" was hired by Nonthal for the job sometime in the 15<sup>th</sup> century <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/DR\" title=\"DR\">DR</a>.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-sewers_6-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-sewers-6\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>6<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Geography\">Geography</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Geography\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Nonthal?veaction=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Geography\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n\n<p>Nonthal stood just north from and connected to the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/Turmway\" title=\"Turmway\">Turmway</a> and the town of <a href=\"/wiki/Centaur_Bridge\" title=\"Centaur Bridge\">Centaur Bridge</a> via a well-traveled road that continued further north towards the towns of <span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvU2FtYnJ5bnR5bj9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\" title=\"Sambryntyn (page does not exist)\">Sambryntyn</span> and <span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvTW9vbmh1bnRfRG93bj9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\" title=\"Moonhunt Down (page does not exist)\">Moonhunt Down</span> a bit further.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-poly103_7-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-poly103-7\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>7<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Trade\">Trade</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Trade\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Nonthal?veaction=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Trade\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The city's main trade was cattle. Nonthal was surrounded by a strong aroma of <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/Manure\" title=\"Manure\">manure</a>, slaughterhouses, and the chemical stench of its many tanneries.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRCS3-p221_4-3\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS3-p221-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> It served as a market town for smaller farming communities that were sprinkled around Nonthal.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-poly106_5-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-poly106-5\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"History\">History</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: History\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Nonthal?veaction=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: History\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The city was named after a <a href=\"/wiki/Wizard\" title=\"Wizard\">wizard</a>, who moved there in the early-to-mid 13th-century <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/DR\" title=\"DR\">DR</a>. He built his cottage behind an inn and put up signs warning people to leave him alone, then promptly disappeared. His house was quickly ransacked of valuables, and the cottage's stone walls were broken apart to be used elsewhere.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-poly106_5-2\"><a href=\"#cite_note-poly106-5\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> Within the remnants of the home, a map to a ruin called <span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvTm9udGhhbCUyN3NfSG9sZD9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\" title=\"Nonthal's Hold (page does not exist)\">Nonthal's Hold</span> was discovered. The map led to a road behind the <a href=\"/wiki/Three_Trees_Inn\" title=\"Three Trees Inn\">Three Trees Inn</a> at the city's center, a sunken and heavily trapped path, as the people who traversed it quickly found. The Inn was rebuilt so as to give a commanding view of the path and soon became the center of activity in the entire city and its main form of entertainment, as onlookers bet on how far hapless adventurers seeking <span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvTm9udGhhbF8ocGVyc29uKT9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\" title=\"Nonthal (person) (page does not exist)\">Nonthal's</span> fabled stash of <a href=\"/wiki/Gold\" title=\"Gold\">gold</a> got.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Nonthal_3-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Nonthal-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRCG-p184_1-4\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCG-p184-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>At some point in the late 14<sup>th</sup> century DR, a powerful mage named <span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvRmVybl8ocGVyc29uKT9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\" title=\"Fern (person) (page does not exist)\">Fern</span> walked Nonthal's Path, dispelling its <i>portals</i> with his clever spells. When he reached the destination – an old dung hole that held the final <i>portal</i> to the fabled wizard's lair, Fern attempted to dispel it. However, the magic traps were smarter than Fern, and they <i>teleported</i> him to Anauroch, across <a href=\"/wiki/Faer%C3%BBn\" title=\"Faerûn\">Faerûn</a>. This attempt was witnessed and immortalized in writing by Adamar Session, <a href=\"/wiki/Bard\" title=\"Bard\">bard</a> of <a href=\"/wiki/Starmantle\" title=\"Starmantle\">Starmantle</a>. Eventually, Fern returned to Nonthal and could always be found in the Three Trees Inn, plotting further attempts.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-VR-p15_8-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-VR-p15-8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>8<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Notable_Locations\">Notable Locations</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Notable Locations\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Nonthal?veaction=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Notable Locations\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><i><span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvMTNfR2F0ZXNfb2ZfTWFnaWM/YWN0aW9uPWVkaXQmcmVkbGluaz0x\" title=\"13 Gates of Magic (page does not exist)\">13 Gates of Magic</span></i>, a set of <i><a href=\"/wiki/Portal\" title=\"Portal\">portal</a></i> traps that guarded Nonthal's Hold, scattered every three steps along Nonthal's Path. Without uttering correct passwords for each, they spirited unwitting adventures to <a href=\"/wiki/Yliyl\" title=\"Yliyl\">Yliyl</a> of Anauroch, <a href=\"/wiki/Whitehorn\" title=\"Whitehorn\">Whitehorn</a> mountains of <a href=\"/wiki/Thar\" title=\"Thar\">Thar</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Dlathilvaer\" title=\"Dlathilvaer\">Dlathilvaer</a> of <a href=\"/wiki/Evereska\" title=\"Evereska\">Evereska</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/Serpent\" title=\"Serpent\">serpent</a>-infested location in <a href=\"/wiki/Chult\" title=\"Chult\">Chult</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Halruaa\" title=\"Halruaa\">Halruaa</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Underdark\" title=\"Underdark\">Underdark</a>, among others.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-poly106_5-3\"><a href=\"#cite_note-poly106-5\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvTm9udGhhbCUyN3NfSG9sZD9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\" title=\"Nonthal's Hold (page does not exist)\">Nonthal's Hold</span>, the hidden lair of the wizard Nonthal, protected by a series of magical <i><a href=\"/wiki/Teleport\" title=\"Teleport\">teleporting</a></i> traps along Nonthl's Path. The hold itself was rumored to be hidden in <a href=\"/wiki/Feywild\" title=\"Feywild\">Feywild</a>,<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRCG-p184_1-5\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCG-p184-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> and contained powerful <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/Enchanted\" title=\"Enchanted\">enchanted</a> items and <a href=\"/wiki/Spellbook\" title=\"Spellbook\">spellbooks</a>.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-poly106_5-4\"><a href=\"#cite_note-poly106-5\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvTm9udGhhbCUyN3NfUGF0aD9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\" title=\"Nonthal's Path (page does not exist)\">Nonthal's Path</span>, the road that began in the center of the city and led towards the magically-hidden Nonthal's Hold, beyond a misused dung-pit.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRCG-p184_1-6\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCG-p184-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-poly106_5-5\"><a href=\"#cite_note-poly106-5\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Three_Trees_Inn\" title=\"Three Trees Inn\">Three Trees Inn</a>, the center of most activities in the city and the main lodging available for ambitious gold-seekers. Individuals who were brave enough to walk Nonthal's Path were a major entertainment for the guests of the inn.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Nonthal_3-2\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Nonthal-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Inhabitants\">Inhabitants</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Inhabitants\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Nonthal?veaction=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Inhabitants\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notably, Nonthal had a significant <a href=\"/wiki/Gnome\" title=\"Gnome\">gnomish</a> population, reviled only by the city of <a href=\"/wiki/Xorhun\" title=\"Xorhun\">Xorhun</a>.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-VR-p21_2-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-VR-p21-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> Many of them were <i><a href=\"/wiki/Illusionist\" title=\"Illusionist\">illusionists</a></i> by trade and made a living entertaining and pranking travelers with sparkling lights and raucous sounds.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Nonthal_3-3\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Nonthal-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Appendix\">Appendix</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Appendix\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Nonthal?veaction=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Appendix\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Gallery\">Gallery</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Gallery\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Nonthal?veaction=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Gallery\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<div class=\"wikia-gallery wikia-gallery-caption-below wikia-gallery-position-left wikia-gallery-spacing-medium wikia-gallery-border-small wikia-gallery-captions-left wikia-gallery-caption-size-medium\" data-seq-no=\"0\" hash=\"d3430e70b3f097a908413e5aa62aa42b\" id=\"gallery-0\"><div class=\"wikia-gallery-caption\"></div><div class=\"wikia-gallery-item\" style=\"width:187px; \"><div class=\"lightbox-caption\" style=\"width:185px;\"><i>A map of <a href=\"/wiki/Turmish\" title=\"Turmish\">Turmish</a> circa late 14<sup>th</sup> century <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/DR\" title=\"DR\">DR</a>.</i></div></div><div class=\"wikia-gallery-item\" style=\"width:187px; \"><div class=\"lightbox-caption\" style=\"width:185px;\"><i>A detailed map of Turmish and its many towns and roads.</i></div></div></div>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Appearances\">Appearances</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Appearances\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Nonthal?veaction=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Appearances\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<dl><dd><dl><dt>Novels</dt>\n